    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0147" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00/834: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-16T23:00:00+03:00">April 16, 1939—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 16—8:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>184. Following is the text in translation of telegram from Kalinin<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d123-f1"/> to the President released to the press tonight: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Mr. President: I consider it a pleasant duty to express to you deep
                            sympathy as well as hearty congratulations in regard to the noble appeal
                            which you have sent to the Governments of Germany and Italy. You may be
                            sure that your initiative finds the warmest response in the hearts of
                            the peoples of the Soviet Socialist Union who are sincerely interested
                            in the preservation of universal peace. Signed Kalinin.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d123-f1" n="8" xml:id="d123-f1-content">
                <p>President of the Presidium of the Supreme Council of the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
